Copy this file to crashbox-dsn.local (gitignored) and put the dedicated
Seedbed Crashbox DSN in it, on one line, for a distributed pilot build.

    https://<public-key>@<crashbox-host>/<project-uuid>

Never commit the real file. Packaging refuses to continue if this file and the
hosted-Sentry fallback file are both populated, so a release has exactly one
destination and never dual-sends.

Without either local file the packaged app carries an empty reporting address
and cannot send anything regardless of the user preference. Roll back by
removing this file, restoring sentry-dsn.local, rebuilding the exact prior
source commit, and repeating the same one-event proof before distribution.
